course: dictionary
lesson: 1925
title: Comfortably in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Comfortably tells you how something is done. It comes from comfort, so it often means in a relaxed, easy way. To find the right meaning, look at the words around it. «The stoats grumbled that the weasels would stop comfortably in the banqueting-hall, and have feasting and toasts and songs, while they guarded in the cold and the dark.» The stoats are out in the cold and dark, so comfortably must mean in a warm, pleasant, easy way.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «Would stop in a warm, pleasant way» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Comfortably can also mean easily, as in «won comfortably», or with enough money, as in «comfortably off». The clues around the word decide which one it is.
fact: Comfortably is an adverb: it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Comfortably» can mean in a relaxed way, free from pain or worry, as in «sitting comfortably».
fact: «Comfortably» can mean easily, with plenty to spare, as in «They won comfortably» in a sports report.
fact: «Comfortably off» means having enough money to live well, with no money worries.
fact: The storytime line «Are you sitting comfortably? Then I'll begin» uses the first meaning.
exercise: «Are you sitting comfortably? Then I'll begin.» What does comfortably mean here? | With a pen | *In a relaxed way, free from pain or worry | Very quickly | Loudly and proudly
exercise: «They won comfortably.» In a sports report, what does this mean? | They were very tired after the game | Only just, by one point | *By a big margin, with plenty to spare | They cheated to win
exercise: «The Smiths are comfortably off.» What does this tell you? | They are poor and hungry | They are very rich and famous | They live in a tent | *They have enough money to live well, with no money worries
test: In maths, «the box comfortably fits in the bag» means | *There is room left over | The box is empty | The bag is broken | The box is too big for the bag
test: Which phrase means having enough money to live well? | *comfortably off | sit comfortably | win comfortably | fit comfortably
exam: In «the weasels would stop comfortably in the banqueting-hall, while the stoats were cold outside», what does comfortably mean? | Only just, with barely any room | Quickly and noisily | *Warm, pleasant and at ease | Angrily, with a grumble
